commit fe96e442f4f2bce79a6c548ec0d714cf34812210
Author: fujiwarat <takao.fujiwara1@gmail.com>
Date:   2019-04-11 19:31:11 +0900

    src-worddic: infinite loop if the end of anthy journal file is broken
    
    Normally the end of anthy journal file, $CONFIG/last-record2_default.utf8,
    should be '\n' when we check it with 'od' command.
    But if that file is broken, the end of file would not be '\n'
    and anthy_do_create_context() could go into an infinite loop.
    
    The solution is to check EOF besides '\n' in record.c:read_1_token().
    
    BUG=https://ja.osdn.net/projects/anthy/ticket/33075
    BUG=https://groups.google.com/forum/#!topic/ibus-user/eRr0Ix4GbgE

M	src-worddic/record.c

